  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social Media Campaign on Peaceful Youth in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A) Establish a gender -responsive community of practice for key influencers across Ethiopia to dialogue and identify how to prevent violent conflict and peacebuilding responses from conflict affected urban and rural areas of Ethiopia.  B) Conduct and disseminate the findings of action -oriented research (e.g., policy briefs, a position paper), in collaboration with experts, to build national consensus around gender -responsive peacebuilding for the National Dialogue Commission.  C) Facilitate inclusive localized community level dialogues among displaced and host communities from Northern Ethiopia to advance social cohesion, while providing a platform where women and youth have a voice that can be brought forward to the National Dialogue Commission.  D) Create and facilitate a consultative insider -mediation platform where local women leaders connect with Civil Society (CS)/Government leaders and influence public opinion for gender -responsive peacebuilding at national level.  E) Coordinate meetings and advocacy actions (e.g., joint letters, statements and recommendations) to situate women leaders at key regional African Union (AU) influencing spaces for gender -responsive mediation and resolution efforts of the Northern Ethiopia crisis.  F) Organize a national policy roundtable with key stakeholders to outline recommendations on building women&apos;s voice and leadership in the National Dialogue Commission.  Oxfam Hong Kong (OHK) will be covering the budget for the following activities to be implemented this year.   - Organizing Social Media Campaign on peaceful Youth   -  Conducting an action -oriented research on building national consensus around gender and youth responsive peace building  - Organizing 2 community level dialogue forums on peace in Addis Ababa    - Train Oxfam staff and partners on the basics of peace building and conflict prevention  For FY 23 -24 the aim is to contribute to peacebuilding, togetherness, and environmental consciousness through a series of physical</narrative>
  </description>
